WEBVTT

00:10.010 --> 00:12.846
[helicopter whirring]

00:14.639 --> 00:17.851
[zombies growling]

00:25.608 --> 00:27.569
-[gasps]
-Whoa!

00:27.652 --> 00:30.196
[suspenseful music]

00:36.202 --> 00:37.787
[growling]

00:43.293 --> 00:45.962
The kids getting bullied
are a problem too.

00:46.046 --> 00:48.715
Honestly, the kids must have
a reason for bullying you.

00:50.717 --> 00:51.968
[snarls]

00:53.428 --> 00:54.763
Look.

00:54.846 --> 00:56.556
-It's okay. Take it off.
-[Eun-ji whimpering]

00:56.639 --> 00:58.391
-Hands off.
-Don't you dare move.

00:58.892 --> 01:00.935
[helicopter whirring]

01:03.688 --> 01:05.023
[gasps]

01:05.607 --> 01:06.566
You did nothing wrong?

01:10.153 --> 01:12.072
Nothing you feel bad about?

01:14.032 --> 01:16.993
Honestly, the kids must have
a reason for bullying you.

01:18.244 --> 01:21.122
PROVIDING AN EDUCATION
THAT WARMS AND STRENGTHENS LIVES

01:29.547 --> 01:31.633
You know, I really wish the school
would burn down.

01:32.967 --> 01:34.385
[Eun-ji] Till nothing's left.

01:35.428 --> 01:36.805
So that everything will be gone.

01:38.765 --> 01:40.600
[flame roaring]

01:40.683 --> 01:42.894
[snarling]

01:48.024 --> 01:51.236
-[growling]
-[grunts]

01:52.946 --> 01:54.197
Hey, Dae-su!

01:55.115 --> 01:57.117
[action music]

01:58.201 --> 01:59.452
[grunts]

02:00.912 --> 02:03.206
[squelching]

02:03.289 --> 02:06.126
What about others? Is it really just you?

02:06.209 --> 02:07.085
I'm by myself.

02:07.168 --> 02:09.170
What about downstairs? In the classrooms?

02:09.254 --> 02:11.256
There's no one down there. It's just me!

02:12.507 --> 02:13.591
[grunts]

02:18.429 --> 02:19.430
[grunts]

02:23.351 --> 02:25.311
-[breathing heavily]
-[Dae-su] Hold tight!

02:26.146 --> 02:28.439
You're sure? There's no one else, right?

02:29.232 --> 02:30.567
They're all zombies.

02:32.277 --> 02:33.444
There are no survivors.

02:35.029 --> 02:36.990
-[Joon-yeong] Pull it tighter, guys.
-[grunting]

02:37.073 --> 02:39.075
[helicopter whirring]

02:41.119 --> 02:42.203
[bangs on door]

02:42.287 --> 02:44.539
[tense music]

02:50.295 --> 02:51.963
[helicopter hissing]

02:56.301 --> 02:58.261
[whirring]

03:08.396 --> 03:10.148
Give me your eye, huh?

03:10.231 --> 03:11.983
[groaning]

03:12.567 --> 03:16.571
-[groaning]
-[bones crunching]

03:16.654 --> 03:17.947
What the hell?

03:20.533 --> 03:21.951
Why didn't you die?

03:25.496 --> 03:26.456
[grunts]

03:30.335 --> 03:31.169
[gasps]

03:31.252 --> 03:33.963
[tense music]

03:36.799 --> 03:40.803
[snarling]

03:40.887 --> 03:43.348
[fire whooshing]

03:49.270 --> 03:52.899
[fire crackling]

04:01.658 --> 04:04.577
[alarm ringing, blaring]

04:05.870 --> 04:08.081
DOOR WILL OPEN AUTOMATICALLY
IN CASE OF FIRE

04:08.957 --> 04:10.124
[On-jo] Guys!

04:10.208 --> 04:11.376
The door's unlocked.

04:14.170 --> 04:17.507
-Let's go!
-One, two, three!

04:17.590 --> 04:18.466
[grunts]

04:21.052 --> 04:22.804
-Look! A chopper!
-Over here!

04:22.887 --> 04:24.597
-Help!
-Hey!

04:24.681 --> 04:25.556
[On-jo] Over here!

04:25.640 --> 04:26.766
[Dae-su] We're here!

04:26.849 --> 04:28.268
[Hyo-ryeong] Help!

04:28.351 --> 04:29.852
Come back!

04:29.936 --> 04:31.229
-Help!
-Come back!

04:31.312 --> 04:33.982
[all shouting]

04:34.065 --> 04:37.568
[engine whirring]

04:45.827 --> 04:49.247
[all shouting]

04:49.330 --> 04:50.957
[Wu-jin] Where are you going?

04:51.040 --> 04:52.542
[all] Help!

04:52.625 --> 04:54.627
[suspenseful music]

04:57.630 --> 04:59.966
[students shouting]

05:01.592 --> 05:03.594
-Hey!
-[crying]

05:03.678 --> 05:05.263
[Joon-yeong] Over here!

05:05.346 --> 05:07.181
[crying]

05:07.265 --> 05:09.726
-[helicopter whirring]
-We're here!

05:12.729 --> 05:16.190
[panting]

05:16.274 --> 05:18.359
[somber music]

05:22.155 --> 05:24.782
[alarm ringing]

05:24.866 --> 05:27.118
[water trickling]

05:30.663 --> 05:33.666
[snarling]

05:33.750 --> 05:36.044
[suspenseful music]

05:39.797 --> 05:41.716
[Hyo-ryeong] Mom…

05:43.968 --> 05:46.846
[sobbing]

05:52.185 --> 05:55.104
[banging on door]

05:56.355 --> 05:57.273
[Hyo-ryeong] Mom…

05:57.940 --> 06:02.653
[banging on door]

06:04.072 --> 06:06.074
[suspenseful music]

06:21.172 --> 06:23.883
[banging continues]

06:33.726 --> 06:35.645
[zombies snarling]

06:37.480 --> 06:38.439
Fuck it.

06:46.155 --> 06:47.240
He's gone.

06:47.865 --> 06:49.450
What the actual fuck?

06:51.327 --> 06:53.246
-Who's gone?
-Gwi-nam.

06:55.790 --> 06:56.999
It's his smell.

06:57.917 --> 06:59.418
[Nam-ra] I hear his breathing.

07:07.593 --> 07:09.595
[theme music]

07:11.097 --> 07:14.308
[squelching]

07:24.527 --> 07:27.530
[all snarling]

07:27.613 --> 07:29.615
HYOSAN HIGH SCHOOL

07:29.699 --> 07:31.826
[car hissing]

07:40.168 --> 07:42.420
[birds chirping]

07:49.719 --> 07:51.721
[tense music]

07:51.804 --> 07:53.973
[bicycle rattling]

08:01.814 --> 08:04.692
What happened?
Didn't Gwi-nam fall from the fourth floor?

08:04.775 --> 08:05.902
Yeah, I threw him off.

08:05.985 --> 08:07.737
So how did he manage to survive?

08:07.820 --> 08:08.988
[sighs]

08:11.032 --> 08:13.951
Maybe he doesn't die.
He comes back to life.

08:15.870 --> 08:17.663
He's not a human or a zombie.

08:20.458 --> 08:22.543
Do you remember that girl
in the teachers' office?

08:22.627 --> 08:23.836
I'm gonna kill you!

08:23.920 --> 08:26.339
Give it to me, you fucker! I'll kill you!

08:29.091 --> 08:31.427
-Yeah, she was weird.
-He's like her, isn't he?

08:32.762 --> 08:33.638
You could be right.

08:35.806 --> 08:37.391
Maybe Nam-ra is the same.

08:39.936 --> 08:41.145
[Dae-su] Look, I found an "O."

08:42.146 --> 08:43.940
[Ji-min] That's what you've got?

08:44.732 --> 08:45.816
She'll be okay.

08:46.442 --> 08:48.152
You can't guarantee that'll happen.

08:49.987 --> 08:52.031
We can't guarantee
anything right now, can we?

08:52.865 --> 08:54.909
We don't even know if we're gonna live.

08:55.451 --> 08:56.744
Let's go make the SOS sign.

08:59.539 --> 09:00.498
Bare-su.

09:03.084 --> 09:06.003
What if it were On-jo,
could you just abandon her?

09:06.587 --> 09:08.589
[tense music]

09:15.304 --> 09:17.223
It came and left, huh? The helicopter?

09:17.932 --> 09:18.808
Mm-hm.

09:19.517 --> 09:22.019
Maybe they started the rescues.
Let's get to the roof.

09:22.770 --> 09:24.522
What if that's the end of the rescue?

09:24.605 --> 09:25.815
Maybe it's only the beginning.

09:26.691 --> 09:28.776
We don't even know if it'll come back.

09:28.859 --> 09:30.736
I don't think we should try
to go up to the roof.

09:30.820 --> 09:33.281
[Mi-jin] What if it does come back?
What then?

09:33.364 --> 09:34.615
-Nothing.
-Yeah, right.

09:36.117 --> 09:37.827
We can't make it to the roof, anyway.

09:39.453 --> 09:40.871
How are we gonna carry him up there?

09:40.955 --> 09:43.082
[groans]
Yep.

09:44.125 --> 09:46.752
-Just leave me and go.
-For real?

09:47.378 --> 09:49.380
Yeah. You should just go.

09:50.006 --> 09:52.049
You mean it? You know me, right?

09:53.175 --> 09:54.552
I'll do it.

09:55.261 --> 09:56.512
Should we?

09:57.054 --> 09:57.930
Shouldn't we?

09:59.640 --> 10:00.683
Don't act all tough.

10:00.766 --> 10:02.560
There are enough crazy tough guys outside.

10:02.643 --> 10:05.605
I'm not gonna die from this, am I?

10:06.480 --> 10:08.649
[sighs]
How would I know if you'll die?

10:09.483 --> 10:11.819
Anyway, I think we should put up
a sign or something outside.

10:11.902 --> 10:14.155
How's anyone going to know
if we're in here and save us?

10:14.238 --> 10:17.199
Doesn't this place have a roof?
Can't you just get there?

10:18.326 --> 10:19.744
They'll see us on the roof.

10:19.827 --> 10:22.538
Well, there is a ladder
that leads to the roof, but--

10:22.622 --> 10:24.415
There is, right? Where is it?

10:24.498 --> 10:25.750
-It's outside.
-Outside?

10:25.833 --> 10:26.792
Yeah, outside.

10:26.876 --> 10:30.129
[zombies snarling]

10:30.212 --> 10:33.257
-Motherfucker. Get over here!
-Wait, wait, wait. Why?

10:33.341 --> 10:34.759
-Outside? Outside?
-Oh.

10:34.842 --> 10:35.718
-Sorry!
-Get back here.

10:35.801 --> 10:37.136
-[groans]
-Stay back.

10:37.219 --> 10:38.262
[Mi-jin] Get your ass here.

10:38.346 --> 10:40.473
-I'll put you outside for five seconds!
-[Min-jae] Help!

10:40.556 --> 10:41.432
This is too big.

10:41.515 --> 10:42.558
How about this?

10:43.142 --> 10:44.685
-Break it apart.
-Here's a big one.

10:44.769 --> 10:46.020
How's this?

10:46.604 --> 10:47.813
Not that one. Put it down.

10:47.897 --> 10:48.981
Not this?

10:49.065 --> 10:51.442
-Grab anything big and colorful.
-[Hyo-ryeong] Can I use this?

10:51.525 --> 10:53.778
[Wu-jin] Joon-yeong, go up there and look.

10:54.612 --> 10:55.821
[Hyo-ryeong] Careful. Careful.

10:55.905 --> 10:57.031
[grunts]

10:57.823 --> 10:58.866
[Ji-min] How does it look?

10:58.949 --> 11:00.660
-First…
-[Hyo-ryeong] Yes.

11:00.743 --> 11:02.286
The "O," it's just too narrow.

11:02.370 --> 11:05.122
He said the "O" is too narrow.
Dae-su, hand me that long one.

11:05.748 --> 11:07.917
[On-jo] It should be
much bigger than this.

11:09.043 --> 11:10.419
Nam-ra, could you carry this?

11:11.754 --> 11:13.047
[Wu-jin] Guys, keep it up.

11:13.130 --> 11:14.382
That goes over there.

11:14.465 --> 11:15.341
It goes like this.

11:15.424 --> 11:18.219
-And the "S" is way too short.
-[Dae-su] We need one more of these.

11:18.302 --> 11:21.430
-[Hyo-ryeong] Is this enough?
-Fill that spot in too. That's it.

11:21.514 --> 11:23.140
[Hyo-ryeong] Oh, I, I got this part.

11:24.058 --> 11:25.142
They're too close.

11:25.226 --> 11:26.727
Hey, spread that out a little bit.

11:26.811 --> 11:28.104
[On-jo] Let's clean it up a bit.

11:28.187 --> 11:30.523
Come take a look. We did a good job, guys.

11:31.440 --> 11:32.316
Look.

11:32.400 --> 11:34.610
Yeah, well, there's no way
anyone can miss that.

11:35.486 --> 11:37.321
-[Dae-su] Right?
-[Wu-jin] We did do a good job.

11:37.405 --> 11:39.407
[dramatic music]

11:41.992 --> 11:43.953
[Hyo-ryeong]
It's a little crooked, though.

11:44.036 --> 11:45.079
[Byeong-chan sighs]

11:45.162 --> 11:46.497
[Byeong-chan] Hope is…

11:47.498 --> 11:51.836
the cruelest torture that prevents you
from giving up on life entirely.

11:51.919 --> 11:54.922
[zombies grunting]

11:55.005 --> 11:57.591
[zombies growling]

11:57.675 --> 11:59.427
[chain clinking]

12:02.430 --> 12:06.434
REALTY

12:06.517 --> 12:08.978
[tense music]

12:14.442 --> 12:18.195
WOOGYEONG GIRL'S MIDDLE SCHOOL

12:18.279 --> 12:19.280
HYOSAN ARTS CENTER

12:20.739 --> 12:24.243
I can't think of anything else,
but I also can't stop trying.

12:27.580 --> 12:29.123
MYEONHAK-DONG

12:30.374 --> 12:32.168
HYOSAN HIGH SCHOOL

12:32.251 --> 12:33.461
[paper rustling]

12:33.544 --> 12:35.546
[suspenseful music]

12:44.096 --> 12:46.849
Once the temperature went up,
the white blood cells were activated.

12:47.892 --> 12:51.103
But they were absorbed by the virus
and transformed into a different one.

12:54.732 --> 12:58.235
[zombies growling]

13:02.948 --> 13:05.201
[suspenseful music continues]

13:09.497 --> 13:10.372
Careful now.

13:10.456 --> 13:13.751
[groaning]

13:15.544 --> 13:16.587
The zombies…

13:16.670 --> 13:18.380
[mumbles]

13:18.464 --> 13:20.216
[groans]

13:21.175 --> 13:22.301
Get a bite down.

13:23.302 --> 13:26.430
-[groaning]
-You're doing great.

13:29.725 --> 13:32.478
[panting]

13:33.020 --> 13:34.855
No, it's not broken.
[sighs]

13:35.940 --> 13:38.609
So it'll get better soon,
just leave it like this.

13:39.944 --> 13:40.986
Thanks, detective.

13:42.196 --> 13:45.157
No need for formalities
in the middle of all this. Call me Jae-ik.

13:45.783 --> 13:46.617
Okay.

13:47.201 --> 13:49.662
Since we're stuck up here,
and we're getting to know each other,

13:49.745 --> 13:51.372
can I be completely frank with you?

13:51.455 --> 13:53.082
Yes, of course. Say anything you want.

13:53.165 --> 13:54.250
Mm, okay.

13:54.333 --> 13:56.502
-Dumbass. You're such an idiot.
-Aah! Ow!

13:56.585 --> 13:59.463
You came all the way here just to shoot
some stupid Internet show?

13:59.547 --> 14:01.715
You're unbelievably dumb.

14:01.799 --> 14:04.885
What? Like and subscribe?
You like that more than your life?

14:04.969 --> 14:06.929
You're one crazy stupid motherfucker.

14:08.347 --> 14:09.306
I'm sorry, detective.

14:09.390 --> 14:12.142
Don't call me detective.
I said to call me by my name.

14:12.226 --> 14:13.269
It's fine, detective.

14:13.352 --> 14:16.105
If you were my brother,
you wouldn't need to worry about zombies.

14:16.188 --> 14:18.357
I would just beat you to death myself.

14:19.108 --> 14:22.945
But someone has to uncover the real truth
and let the world know what's happening.

14:23.028 --> 14:24.572
What? The truth?

14:25.322 --> 14:27.700
Hey. Are you a journalist?

14:27.783 --> 14:28.659
I…

14:29.201 --> 14:31.871
Well, journalists don't dig hard enough
for the truth, you know?

14:31.954 --> 14:34.081
That's where people like me come in.

14:34.164 --> 14:36.458
[grumbles]
Your excuses.

14:37.293 --> 14:38.127
Oh.

14:38.794 --> 14:42.464
It looked like your colleague
totally dumped you and took off.

14:42.548 --> 14:44.258
Should I blast him on my show?

14:44.341 --> 14:46.051
I can even interview you if you want.

14:47.136 --> 14:49.972
-Forget it.
-You should take revenge on traitors.

14:50.055 --> 14:50.931
Look.

14:51.724 --> 14:54.059
I learned from my many years
as a detective.

14:54.143 --> 14:55.853
The assholes fighting to stay alive,

14:55.936 --> 14:58.647
and assholes coming at you
hoping to die can't be beaten.

14:59.398 --> 15:01.025
[sighs]
I'm worried for the kids.

15:02.359 --> 15:04.194
I have a pretty good number of followers.

15:04.278 --> 15:06.030
I can cancel him socially for good.

15:06.113 --> 15:08.866
-Oysterubbish.
-Orangibberish. Not Oysterubbish.

15:08.949 --> 15:10.784
Who even cares? Just shut up, would you?

15:10.868 --> 15:12.953
And just go pick up
everything we can throw, all right?

15:13.746 --> 15:16.248
-What are you talking about?
-Why else? It's crazy hot up here.

15:16.332 --> 15:19.043
You're gonna stay here
until you become human jerky and die?

15:19.126 --> 15:21.754
Why is everyone I meet like this?

15:22.880 --> 15:25.507
[growling]

15:28.385 --> 15:29.845
They're not moving.

15:29.929 --> 15:32.806
No. The zombies follow sounds.

15:33.641 --> 15:34.725
Another.

15:39.521 --> 15:42.358
-[grunts]
-[metal clanks]

15:42.441 --> 15:44.485
[all snarling]

15:44.568 --> 15:46.320
What are you doing?

15:46.403 --> 15:48.280
You said you'd get rid of them,
not lure them in.

15:48.364 --> 15:50.908
They followed sounds earlier.

15:51.742 --> 15:53.535
Shit. Give me that.

15:53.619 --> 15:55.329
Stop it. More keep coming.

15:55.412 --> 15:56.789
I said you give it to me, asshole.

15:57.539 --> 15:59.291
-I swear you're weird…
-Quick!

16:00.084 --> 16:01.877
[snarling]

16:02.878 --> 16:05.089
[metal clanking]

16:05.172 --> 16:06.840
[car horn honking]

16:06.924 --> 16:08.926
MUNPYEONG DAYCARE

16:09.009 --> 16:11.011
[upbeat music]

16:12.513 --> 16:13.472
Oh, my God.

16:15.432 --> 16:16.266
Oh, my God.

16:19.103 --> 16:19.937
Hey, sergeant!

16:20.020 --> 16:21.772
-You traitor!
-Traitor.

16:23.440 --> 16:26.110
[Ho-cheol] Jump! Jump on top of the bus!

16:26.735 --> 16:27.569
Jump down!

16:27.653 --> 16:29.446
-I got it, asshole. Shh…
-[Ho-cheol] Come on, jump!

16:29.530 --> 16:30.364
-Let's go.
-What?

16:30.990 --> 16:33.200
-I said let's go!
-What… But…

16:37.621 --> 16:39.498
[Ho-cheol] This is freaking me out.

16:42.960 --> 16:44.670
Shit. That was close.

16:44.753 --> 16:46.338
Hey. Jump.

16:46.422 --> 16:48.507
What? I can't jump.

16:48.590 --> 16:50.342
Don't give me that bullshit. Jump.

16:50.426 --> 16:51.760
But I hurt my leg!

16:51.844 --> 16:52.886
I know. Jump!

16:52.970 --> 16:55.931
You should've just taken me with you.
Why did you jump first, huh?

16:56.015 --> 16:58.851
-That's because you're slow! Come on!
-My leg is injured!

16:58.934 --> 17:01.186
You want to die there,
or you want to break your leg here?

17:01.270 --> 17:02.813
-[Ho-cheol] This is nuts.
-[all growling]

17:02.896 --> 17:05.983
But my leg hurts. What about my leg, huh?

17:06.066 --> 17:07.818
-Se-bin.
-Yes?

17:07.901 --> 17:09.820
Close your eyes, keep them shut.

17:09.903 --> 17:11.280
[zombies growling]

17:11.363 --> 17:12.364
[Ho-cheol] Let's just go!

17:12.448 --> 17:14.908
-I'll catch you… Hey, wait, wait!
-No, I can't!

17:14.992 --> 17:16.493
Hold on! Stop! Stop! Stop!

17:16.577 --> 17:18.078
Jump right now, asshole!

17:18.162 --> 17:20.247
Damn it! Hold on. Okay. Hold on.
Just give me a second.

17:20.330 --> 17:21.832
-I'll jump. Wait!
-[Ho-cheol] Just leave him!

17:21.915 --> 17:24.376
Can we just get going for God's sake?

17:24.460 --> 17:25.335
[Jae-ik] Aim for here.

17:25.419 --> 17:27.588
-Shit.
-[Ho-cheol] What the hell are you doing?

17:27.671 --> 17:29.548
[grunting]

17:29.631 --> 17:32.134
Whoa! No! Help me! Help me, detective!

17:32.217 --> 17:35.471
I mean, Jae-ik. Pull me up.
Please save me. Please.

17:35.554 --> 17:37.598
-[whimpering]
-[grunts]

17:37.681 --> 17:38.849
[Ho-cheol] All clear!

17:38.932 --> 17:40.434
Here we go! Hold on tight!

17:40.517 --> 17:42.061
Let's go, Ho-seong!

17:43.062 --> 17:46.440
[Orangibberish] Ooh! Wait!

17:46.523 --> 17:50.360
[Orangibberish shouting]

17:55.532 --> 17:58.410
-What does SOS mean?
-It's a distress signal.

17:58.494 --> 18:01.080
I know that. What does it stand for?

18:01.163 --> 18:04.291
It doesn't stand for anything.
SOS is just SOS.

18:04.374 --> 18:05.918
That makes no sense.

18:06.627 --> 18:08.587
[On-jo] That's just how it is.
It doesn't mean anything.

18:08.670 --> 18:10.672
Then rescue quickly…

18:11.673 --> 18:14.259
Speed of save… Save?

18:14.843 --> 18:16.512
Why'd you ask
if you're not gonna believe me?

18:16.595 --> 18:18.097
I thought you'd know.

18:18.680 --> 18:21.016
I do know. Look it up.
You'll see I'm right.

18:21.642 --> 18:24.061
Whatever. How can I look it up?
I don't have a phone.

18:24.895 --> 18:25.729
What?

18:27.147 --> 18:29.525
I asked On-jo what SOS mean,

18:29.608 --> 18:32.319
and she said it doesn't mean anything.

18:33.570 --> 18:34.905
Just say you don't know next time.

18:34.988 --> 18:36.198
Well, it's true.

18:36.281 --> 18:37.741
It's true.

18:37.825 --> 18:40.327
-Really?
-Mm-hm. She's totally right.

18:40.994 --> 18:42.538
Why don't you believe her?

18:43.330 --> 18:44.206
Hey, prez.

18:45.457 --> 18:46.333
What does SOS mean?

18:46.416 --> 18:47.876
[sighs]
That jerk!

18:47.960 --> 18:49.086
Forget him. Let him be.

18:51.672 --> 18:52.756
Is it true, though?

18:54.424 --> 18:55.259
What?

18:55.759 --> 18:59.179
Are you sure SOS doesn't mean anything?
Isn't it supposed to be an acronym?

19:00.597 --> 19:02.307
-You don't believe me, either?
-Mm.

19:04.143 --> 19:05.269
[groans]

19:05.352 --> 19:07.354
The sun's setting. Let's start a fire.

19:07.437 --> 19:09.857
[Cheong-san groans]

19:10.941 --> 19:13.485
[wood rasping]

19:14.027 --> 19:15.195
[On-jo] It's setting.

19:16.905 --> 19:18.365
[Wu-jin] I think it's working.

19:18.448 --> 19:19.449
[sighs]

19:20.284 --> 19:21.326
I'm done.

19:21.410 --> 19:23.245
-[Wu-jin] Already?
-[Joon-yeong] Next.

19:23.328 --> 19:24.997
All right. Let's do this.

19:25.080 --> 19:26.498
[wood rasping]

19:30.252 --> 19:31.253
[inhales sharply]

19:31.336 --> 19:33.714
You'll get tired. Slow down.

19:33.797 --> 19:35.716
The fire won't start if he goes slowly.

19:36.508 --> 19:37.342
Do it faster.

19:37.426 --> 19:39.261
Faster. Faster. I said come on, faster!

19:39.344 --> 19:41.054
-Rub it faster!
-[groans]

19:41.722 --> 19:42.806
What is it, cramps?

19:43.557 --> 19:46.185
-My hands. I can't do it.
-I'll do it. Step back.

19:46.268 --> 19:48.145
[wood clattering]

19:49.521 --> 19:52.357
[wood rasping]

19:58.655 --> 20:00.699
-[breathes heavily]
-Hey, should we kill him?

20:01.617 --> 20:02.784
Are you praying?

20:03.660 --> 20:05.662
Stop praying. Try… Stop it.

20:07.664 --> 20:08.957
It's hard. It won't work.

20:10.125 --> 20:11.126
[sighs]

20:13.337 --> 20:14.713
Isn't that smoke?

20:14.796 --> 20:16.048
-Hey. Smoke.
-Smoke!

20:16.131 --> 20:17.090
Hold on.

20:17.174 --> 20:18.842
-Please. Come on.
-[Dae-su] Blow.

20:18.926 --> 20:20.427
-[blows air]
-[Dae-su] Come on, blow.

20:20.510 --> 20:21.887
-Be careful.
-[Dae-su] Blow.

20:21.970 --> 20:23.889
Did it work? Su-hyeok?

20:24.514 --> 20:25.849
-Come on, come on.
-[sighs]

20:25.933 --> 20:26.767
Damn it.

20:26.850 --> 20:28.185
[Su-hyeok] Shit.

20:31.313 --> 20:32.231
Let me try.

20:39.321 --> 20:41.031
-[Nam-ra] Hey.
-You're getting there.

20:42.115 --> 20:42.950
Hey.

20:43.033 --> 20:45.369
[breathing heavily]

20:47.329 --> 20:48.747
Just use this.

20:49.748 --> 20:50.874
[awkward music sting]

20:51.500 --> 20:53.293
[pants]

20:53.377 --> 20:55.087
Well, I smoke sometimes.

21:01.218 --> 21:02.844
You had it this whole time.

21:05.264 --> 21:06.348
You don't want it?

21:09.893 --> 21:10.894
Light it.

21:10.978 --> 21:13.689
MUNPYEONG DAYCARE

21:15.816 --> 21:16.900
[smooches]

21:16.984 --> 21:18.819
[chuckles]

21:21.238 --> 21:22.114
[Jae-ik sighs]

21:23.782 --> 21:25.242
Hey, traitor.

21:25.325 --> 21:26.326
A traitor.

21:26.410 --> 21:28.370
I went back and saved you.

21:28.453 --> 21:31.039
You took the children
and abandoned me with this freak.

21:31.123 --> 21:33.625
I found this bus and came back.

21:33.709 --> 21:36.128
[scoffs]
Seriously, man, use your head.

21:36.211 --> 21:37.129
Asshole.

21:37.921 --> 21:40.632
-Do you have a license to drive a bus?
-Uh, no.

21:40.716 --> 21:42.092
I have a regular license.

21:42.175 --> 21:44.094
I swear I'll kill you once we get there.

21:44.177 --> 21:46.179
Starting with driving without a license…

21:46.263 --> 21:47.889
-Stop, stop, stop the bus!
-Whoa!

21:47.973 --> 21:49.099
[brakes squeal]

21:49.850 --> 21:53.395
What? What was that? It's a zombie, right?

21:53.478 --> 21:55.355
Since when do zombies ride bikes?

21:55.439 --> 21:57.524
-Dumbass. Hey, Oyster.
-It's Orange.

21:57.607 --> 21:58.650
Take the baby.

21:58.734 --> 21:59.735
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Careful.

21:59.818 --> 22:01.111
Be careful. Careful, careful.

22:01.987 --> 22:03.113
Open the door.

22:04.740 --> 22:05.824
[lock clicks]

22:08.535 --> 22:10.412
You pull any shit, I'll fucking kill you.

22:10.495 --> 22:12.205
If I become a zombie,
I'll go only after you.

22:12.289 --> 22:14.708
-I'll bite your neck only. Got it?
-Yeah.

22:14.791 --> 22:16.835
[suspenseful music]

22:19.171 --> 22:20.130
Oh, shit.

22:23.383 --> 22:24.301
Excuse me.

22:25.385 --> 22:26.303
Are you okay?

22:29.514 --> 22:32.017
You weren't bitten or anything.

22:33.393 --> 22:34.311
You're okay, right?

22:36.480 --> 22:37.481
Yes, I'm okay.

22:39.858 --> 22:41.568
Come with us. I'm a cop.

22:43.487 --> 22:44.613
[car horn honking]

22:44.696 --> 22:45.822
Sergeant!

22:45.906 --> 22:47.949
-[gunshots]
-[screams]

22:48.533 --> 22:49.951
[Se-bin] Mr. Detective!

22:50.035 --> 22:50.952
No, no, it's okay!

22:51.036 --> 22:52.954
The soldiers are here. They're soldiers.

22:54.164 --> 22:55.582
We're saved!

22:56.750 --> 22:57.709
What was that?

23:02.923 --> 23:03.924
Hey!

23:04.007 --> 23:04.883
Don't shoot!

23:04.966 --> 23:07.469
I'm a cop. Wait. I'm a cop.

23:08.136 --> 23:10.305
Don't shoot! Here! Huh?

23:10.931 --> 23:15.727
Chin down. Extend your left arm.
Don't stick out your chest too much.

23:15.811 --> 23:17.479
Ooh.
[sighs]

23:17.562 --> 23:18.897
This is so sexy, ooh.

23:21.817 --> 23:23.819
-What's with the face?
-Take this seriously,

23:23.902 --> 23:24.778
or don't do it at all.

23:24.861 --> 23:27.239
Stop being so stuck up
about shooting arrows.

23:27.322 --> 23:28.865
[squeaks]

23:31.743 --> 23:32.869
Yeah. Didn't work.

23:32.953 --> 23:34.204
You thought it was easy?

23:34.913 --> 23:36.790
[sighs]
Anything is easier than studying.

23:36.873 --> 23:39.584
You can get into Seoul University
with good grades.

23:39.668 --> 23:41.503
But if you're just good in archery…

23:42.504 --> 23:43.505
you can't go anywhere.

23:44.172 --> 23:47.551
We can't make the national team,
or get a scholarship to college.

23:49.136 --> 23:50.679
There's nothing left to do.

23:50.762 --> 23:53.348
Stop whining. Everyone knows
you'll make the national team.

23:54.057 --> 23:56.309
You'll go to college
just by shooting arrows.

23:56.393 --> 23:57.561
[twang, thud]

23:58.353 --> 23:59.271
[Mi-jin] Damn it.

24:01.314 --> 24:03.358
[dramatic music]

24:06.486 --> 24:07.696
Are you not?

24:08.321 --> 24:11.032
You didn't make the national team?
No college?

24:15.537 --> 24:16.538
[Mi-jin sighs]

24:18.039 --> 24:20.375
[dramatic music continues]

24:24.171 --> 24:25.130
[sighs]

24:25.672 --> 24:28.008
You won't die
if you don't go to college, you know.

24:31.094 --> 24:32.888
I really love shooting arrows.

24:35.432 --> 24:37.058
All I ever knew was archery.

24:38.727 --> 24:40.270
I don't know what else to do.

24:42.105 --> 24:43.398
As long as I could keep doing it,

24:43.481 --> 24:45.901
I didn't care about colleges
or corporate teams.

24:48.153 --> 24:49.196
But now I…

24:50.488 --> 24:52.657
I've nowhere to go shoot my arrows.

24:56.953 --> 24:58.079
I'm only 19.

25:00.457 --> 25:01.708
But I feel like there's no hope.

25:04.252 --> 25:06.630
If the zombies were to kill
all the archers in the country,

25:06.713 --> 25:08.673
you'll automatically make
the national team.

25:09.925 --> 25:10.800
You're nuts.

25:11.676 --> 25:12.719
That's a good thing?

25:12.802 --> 25:14.054
Hey, it's hope.

25:14.638 --> 25:16.473
At least you have potential
to become something.

25:17.432 --> 25:20.018
Even if I survive,
I'm not getting into college.

25:20.101 --> 25:21.353
CSAT? Fuck.

25:22.354 --> 25:24.064
My answers are always C or D.

25:24.856 --> 25:26.066
Why are they C or D?

25:27.067 --> 25:29.319
C if I'm not sure about it,
and D if I'm clueless.

25:29.402 --> 25:30.528
[groans]

25:30.612 --> 25:32.948
I swear it's like
I avoid all the right answers.

25:35.033 --> 25:35.867
[sighs]

25:35.951 --> 25:39.162
All right. That's enough of that.
It's time to teach me how to shoot arrows.

25:39.829 --> 25:42.457
'Cause even if I totally suck,
it's better than you shooting alone.

25:46.378 --> 25:48.380
[calm music]

25:55.011 --> 25:56.554
[fire whooshing]

25:57.597 --> 25:58.515
[Su-hyeok] Dae-su.

25:59.349 --> 26:00.267
[Dae-su] Yeah?

26:01.268 --> 26:02.394
How was your audition?

26:03.436 --> 26:05.438
[scoffs]
They said I have to lose weight.

26:05.522 --> 26:07.148
[chuckles]

26:07.899 --> 26:09.442
Well, you're a good singer.

26:10.860 --> 26:13.029
Sing for us. I wanna hear it.

26:13.697 --> 26:15.824
Just forget it. I don't want it.

26:16.908 --> 26:18.618
I actually really like that song.

26:20.495 --> 26:21.329
Is that so?

26:21.413 --> 26:22.580
Mm-hm.

26:22.664 --> 26:23.665
Really?

26:23.748 --> 26:24.791
It's really nice.

26:26.543 --> 26:27.377
You sing well.

26:27.460 --> 26:29.254
-[clears throat]
-[Wu-jin] It'll cheer us up.

26:31.840 --> 26:35.468
[singing in Korean]
♪ Let's go once it's over ♪

26:36.636 --> 26:41.016
♪ Let's go anywhere ♪

26:42.017 --> 26:45.186
♪ Once we're done studying
12 hours a day ♪

26:45.937 --> 26:48.523
♪ Once the annoying sounds are over ♪

26:49.024 --> 26:52.861
♪ Let's go hand in hand ♪

26:53.486 --> 26:57.324
-♪ Let's not run ♪
-♪ Let's not run ♪

26:57.907 --> 27:01.661
-♪ Let's try walking slowly ♪
-♪ Let's try walking slowly ♪

27:02.746 --> 27:09.294
♪ Is that drool or sweat pooled
On the book? ♪

27:09.377 --> 27:11.796
-♪ No one notices the plop, plop ♪
-♪ No one notices the plop, plop ♪

27:11.880 --> 27:13.673
-♪ The plop, plop ♪
-♪ The plop, plop ♪

27:13.757 --> 27:17.469
-♪ The falling rain drops ♪
-♪ The falling rain drops ♪

27:18.094 --> 27:22.015
-♪ What is boiling? Simmer, simmer ♪
-♪ What is boiling? Simmer, simmer ♪

27:22.098 --> 27:26.269
-♪ It's Mom's doenjang stew ♪
-♪ It's Mom's doenjang stew ♪

27:26.353 --> 27:30.398
-♪ Mm-hm, a bowl of instant noodles ♪
-♪ Mm-hm, a bowl of instant noodles ♪

27:30.482 --> 27:34.611
♪ In front of the TV
Which plays nothing but static ♪

27:35.779 --> 27:40.867
-♪ Let's go anywhere together ♪
-♪ Let's go anywhere together ♪

27:40.950 --> 27:42.952
[foreboding music]

27:44.454 --> 27:47.374
[all growling]

27:53.046 --> 27:56.883
[bones crunching]

28:02.138 --> 28:05.809
I got to get to the rooftop, damn it.

28:05.892 --> 28:09.896
[snarling]

28:09.979 --> 28:11.981
[discordant music playing]

28:16.694 --> 28:18.405
-[Na-yeon whimpers]
-[doorknob clicks]

28:18.488 --> 28:20.490
[discordant music continues]

28:32.293 --> 28:34.879
[zombie snarling]

28:47.767 --> 28:49.769
[discordant music playing]

28:49.853 --> 28:51.771
[growling]

28:51.855 --> 28:54.399
[snarling]

28:57.652 --> 29:00.029
[discordant music playing]

29:05.410 --> 29:07.954
[zombie snarling]

29:13.710 --> 29:15.712
[ominous music]

29:27.474 --> 29:29.601
[ominous music continues]

29:32.145 --> 29:34.147
-[snarling]
-[whimpers]

29:36.191 --> 29:39.194
[thumping on door]

29:39.277 --> 29:41.905
[panting]

29:47.368 --> 29:48.203
[camera beeps]

29:49.454 --> 29:50.580
[Ji-min] The police…

29:51.873 --> 29:53.583
and firefighters never came.

29:54.375 --> 29:56.628
If anybody is watching this after,

29:58.171 --> 29:59.214
punish them.

30:00.882 --> 30:02.258
All involved.

30:02.342 --> 30:04.302
[Hyo-ryeong] …here with some
of my classmates,

30:04.385 --> 30:05.970
and they're really good to me.

30:06.054 --> 30:07.722
Let me just show you. This is them.

30:11.142 --> 30:12.060
[Wu-jin] Hey, Mom.

30:12.644 --> 30:14.145
I want a raise in allowance.

30:17.190 --> 30:18.733
-Is it ready to go?
-[Wu-jin] Yes.

30:19.567 --> 30:20.527
[clears throat]

30:21.194 --> 30:24.864
[Dae-su] Music and lyrics
by intergalactic superstar Yang Dae-su.

30:26.366 --> 30:28.660
[Singing in Korean]
♪ Chicken tastes better fried ♪

30:28.743 --> 30:30.286
♪ In olive oil ♪

30:30.370 --> 30:33.706
♪ Pork tastes better than soy meat ♪

30:33.790 --> 30:37.418
♪ What makes me laugh, laugh, laugh ♪

30:37.502 --> 30:41.297
♪ Is trans fat ♪

30:41.381 --> 30:42.340
I'm hungry.

30:42.423 --> 30:45.134
[Wu-jin] How can you sing
at a time like this?

30:45.218 --> 30:48.596
[Wu-jin] Doesn't it feel like everyone
should leave a final message?

30:49.347 --> 30:51.182
[Dae-su] Why is it final? Are we dying?

30:53.893 --> 30:54.936
[Joon-yeong] Hello.

30:55.019 --> 30:58.731
I'm Oh Joon-yeong, business major
at Seoul University, class of 23.

31:00.233 --> 31:01.693
I'll meet you soon, upperclassmen.

31:01.776 --> 31:04.571
And if I get in, I definitely wanna
find myself a girlfriend.

31:04.654 --> 31:05.613
Won't happen.

31:05.697 --> 31:07.115
[Joon-yeong] What the hell?

31:09.909 --> 31:10.743
[Cheong-san] Mom.

31:12.036 --> 31:12.996
It's me.

31:13.830 --> 31:15.123
Dad, you're okay too, right?

31:17.542 --> 31:21.170
Mom. Listen. Don't freak out, okay?

31:22.672 --> 31:24.966
You're the only person I can tell.

31:26.175 --> 31:27.760
Gyeong-su's dead, Mom.

31:30.388 --> 31:31.764
Because I called him over.

31:35.518 --> 31:37.770
I did it in case he'd bite
the others, but…

31:39.856 --> 31:41.482
It's my fault he died, you know?

31:41.566 --> 31:43.651
[somber music]

31:46.946 --> 31:50.408
Please tell his grandma on my behalf.

31:53.369 --> 31:55.413
Put it gently, so she doesn't get…

31:56.873 --> 31:58.166
too upset.

32:03.838 --> 32:06.424
Gyeong-su wanted to work
at our restaurant, remember?

32:09.802 --> 32:13.139
But I told him no, because he'd try
to eat free chicken every day.

32:13.222 --> 32:14.724
[sobs]

32:16.351 --> 32:19.103
[sobbing]
I should have just let him do it.

32:19.187 --> 32:21.105
[camera beeping]

32:24.484 --> 32:26.778
[somber music continues]

32:30.448 --> 32:33.868
PTA DONATIONS

32:35.787 --> 32:37.789
[ominous music]

32:43.544 --> 32:44.837
[Nam-ra] You killed him.

32:44.921 --> 32:47.548
You wiped that blood
with your handkerchief.

32:47.632 --> 32:49.884
You wiped that on the scratches
on Gyeong-su's hand.

32:50.510 --> 32:52.011
Like his blood is so clean?

32:52.929 --> 32:54.055
He was a zombie.

32:55.682 --> 32:57.308
Nam-ra, that's enough.

32:57.392 --> 33:01.437
It's true. Na-yeon did it. She killed him.

33:01.521 --> 33:03.690
How could you, you're just a fucking…

33:03.773 --> 33:05.108
-How could…
-No!

33:06.401 --> 33:07.360
You're…

33:08.361 --> 33:09.612
a murderer.

33:11.656 --> 33:13.658
[gloomy music]

33:22.208 --> 33:23.835
[music fades]

33:26.379 --> 33:29.257
-Go.
-[Gyeong-su] You killed me.

33:30.174 --> 33:31.426
[Na-yeon] Go.

33:31.509 --> 33:33.094
Please go.

33:33.886 --> 33:35.304
[Gyeong-su] You killed me.

33:37.557 --> 33:39.183
[rustles, thuds]

33:41.310 --> 33:43.396
[gloomy music continues]

33:46.482 --> 33:48.860
[breathing heavily]

34:00.204 --> 34:01.998
[fire whooshing]

34:04.000 --> 34:05.376
It was such a nice song.

34:06.294 --> 34:07.587
Didn't you say that it sucked?

34:08.713 --> 34:11.340
Well, now that I actually listened to it,
I think it's kind of nice.

34:12.133 --> 34:13.760
[Wu-jin] That was encouraging, Dae-su.

34:13.843 --> 34:15.011
[chuckles]

34:18.056 --> 34:19.057
How long…

34:20.308 --> 34:21.809
have you been smoking for?

34:24.270 --> 34:25.730
Since eighth grade.

34:26.481 --> 34:29.233
I had no friends
and a lot of stress back then.

34:31.360 --> 34:33.446
[fire crackling]

34:35.031 --> 34:37.241
Did you ever need a friend, though?

34:38.201 --> 34:39.285
I'm not sure.

34:40.536 --> 34:41.746
I can't really tell.

34:44.749 --> 34:46.542
You always put up a wall.

34:48.878 --> 34:51.547
You'd wear your headphones all day,
and you never said anything.

34:54.300 --> 34:56.219
Wasn't it because you hated us?

34:57.678 --> 34:59.388
[fire crackling]

35:03.226 --> 35:05.269
[fire crackling continues]

35:07.605 --> 35:09.565
I never hated you guys.

35:12.860 --> 35:13.778
I just…

35:16.405 --> 35:18.074
didn't have any friends.

35:19.700 --> 35:20.618
Well…

35:22.036 --> 35:23.913
I never really liked you.

35:23.996 --> 35:26.082
[dramatic music]

35:28.709 --> 35:31.879
I thought you didn't talk to us,
because we were beneath you.

35:33.089 --> 35:34.173
I kind of hated you.

35:35.800 --> 35:38.177
There were times that I wished
you just disappear.

35:40.429 --> 35:43.558
Aren't you close?
You're the top two students.

35:43.641 --> 35:45.143
That's why I hated her.

35:45.226 --> 35:47.520
No matter how hard I worked,
I was always second.

35:49.522 --> 35:50.690
But it's okay now.

35:52.191 --> 35:55.111
I think I was able to come in second,
because of Nam-ra.

35:57.238 --> 35:59.949
Hey. Second's good too.

36:01.576 --> 36:04.453
I can't even be 20th. Right?

36:05.580 --> 36:06.998
-Hey.
-[hands thud]

36:07.081 --> 36:09.625
Don't compare yourself to Joon-yeong.

36:09.709 --> 36:11.085
I was just saying.

36:12.044 --> 36:14.714
Why do you always get on my case
whenever I say something?

36:14.797 --> 36:17.216
[dramatic music continues]

36:17.300 --> 36:19.510
Wait a second. Do you like me?

36:20.678 --> 36:22.847
-Shut up, you moron!
-[chuckles]

36:23.472 --> 36:25.933
[Dae-su] I'm going to put it out there,
so you don't get hurt.

36:27.185 --> 36:28.603
I like somebody else.

36:29.270 --> 36:30.396
So don't like me.

36:30.479 --> 36:32.773
I don't like you!

36:32.857 --> 36:35.151
I'm not interested in you at all.

36:35.234 --> 36:37.445
Dae-su. Who do you like, then?

36:37.528 --> 36:39.488
He's, he's a total freak.

36:41.365 --> 36:43.743
-His sister.
-Ha-ri from Archery?

36:44.327 --> 36:45.912
[Ji-min] You're insane.

36:45.995 --> 36:48.080
[Dae-su] I go crazy when I'm in love.

36:48.164 --> 36:50.833
She's like my little Cupid.

36:50.917 --> 36:52.752
[Wu-jin laughs]
Stop it.

36:52.835 --> 36:55.755
If we get out of here alive,
I'm gonna tell my sister.

36:56.422 --> 36:57.590
Will you really tell her?

36:57.673 --> 36:58.591
-[Wu-jin] Yeah.
-What?

36:58.674 --> 36:59.800
To shoot and kill you.

37:00.426 --> 37:01.636
I said not to like my sister.

37:01.719 --> 37:04.680
You can't do that to me,
future brother-in-law.

37:04.764 --> 37:05.598
[Wu-jin] You… Hey!

37:05.681 --> 37:07.683
-[Dae-su] Will you tell her? Promise?
-[Wu-jin] Yeah. To kill you.

37:07.767 --> 37:10.478
-[Dae-su] Stop it. Seriously. I love her.
-[Wu-jin groans]

37:14.482 --> 37:16.484
[ominous music]

37:17.526 --> 37:19.070
[growling]

37:20.863 --> 37:22.198
Gyeong-su…

37:27.370 --> 37:28.412
No!

37:28.496 --> 37:30.623
[screaming]

37:32.458 --> 37:34.168
[whimpering]

37:34.252 --> 37:35.836
[screams]

37:37.380 --> 37:40.299
[ominous music continues]

37:41.425 --> 37:43.678
[snarling]

37:45.137 --> 37:47.556
-[whimpers]
-[grunts]

37:51.769 --> 37:54.272
[growling]

38:01.070 --> 38:03.489
[pants, screams]

38:06.242 --> 38:08.703
[growling]

38:12.081 --> 38:12.915
[crunches]

38:14.041 --> 38:15.209
[whimpers]

38:19.880 --> 38:20.840
[Na-yeon] Ms. Park.

38:21.882 --> 38:22.883
It's Gyeong-su.

38:24.302 --> 38:26.470
They're all… Gyeong-su.

38:27.138 --> 38:28.180
Na-yeon.

38:28.264 --> 38:30.725
[whimpering]

38:31.684 --> 38:34.437
You were scared.
So were the others. That's all.

38:35.604 --> 38:38.482
So make sure you go back to them later.

38:40.526 --> 38:44.196
Go to them and tell them…

38:46.407 --> 38:47.783
and tell Gyeong-su

38:49.243 --> 38:50.453
that you're sorry.

38:51.120 --> 38:52.747
[sobbing]

38:53.831 --> 38:54.790
Na-yeon.

38:56.375 --> 38:57.293
Stay alive.

38:59.253 --> 39:00.212
You have to stay alive.

39:00.296 --> 39:02.340
[somber music]

39:03.966 --> 39:06.302
And you're gonna help them
this time. Okay?

39:08.429 --> 39:12.058
Do at least one thing to help them,
you understand?

39:13.100 --> 39:14.810
[groaning]

39:17.146 --> 39:19.774
[sobbing]

39:19.857 --> 39:21.901
[groaning]

39:23.944 --> 39:27.448
[bones crunching]

39:28.824 --> 39:30.618
[groaning]

39:31.369 --> 39:33.079
-[Sun-hwa] Na-yeon.
-[sobbing]

39:33.954 --> 39:36.791
It wasn't your fault.

39:37.750 --> 39:39.043
It was my fault.

39:42.004 --> 39:43.881
I'm sorry for cornering you.

39:45.091 --> 39:46.842
[groans]

39:47.593 --> 39:49.678
[somber music continues]

39:53.974 --> 39:55.559
[whimpers]

39:57.186 --> 39:58.145
You…

39:59.605 --> 40:03.234
Na-yeon, you have to stay alive.

40:03.317 --> 40:05.528
[breathing heavily]

40:09.573 --> 40:13.327
[groaning]

40:14.578 --> 40:16.580
[somber music]

40:26.549 --> 40:29.093
[somber music rises]

40:34.557 --> 40:35.683
[music fades]

40:36.642 --> 40:38.936
[pensive music]

40:55.494 --> 40:57.538
[pensive music continues]

41:11.760 --> 41:16.432
INSTRUMENT STORAGE

41:17.600 --> 41:19.602
[ominous music]

41:28.360 --> 41:31.906
[Ji-min] My mom and dad prepped
everything for my transfer.

41:33.449 --> 41:34.867
They said to just go to Seoul.

41:37.203 --> 41:39.038
But I really didn't want to go there.

41:39.121 --> 41:40.998
[fire crackling]

41:42.750 --> 41:46.587
I wouldn't have had any friends,
and I was afraid of the Seoul kids.

41:48.172 --> 41:49.840
I didn't know what to do.

41:52.218 --> 41:54.345
Then On-jo gave me a great idea.

41:57.515 --> 42:00.100
She said I just had to cut school
for five days.

42:01.685 --> 42:04.063
Then the principal can't write you
a recommendation.

42:05.940 --> 42:07.274
So that's what I did.

42:10.319 --> 42:11.904
It's all thanks to On-jo…

42:14.073 --> 42:15.783
that I didn't have to transfer.

42:15.866 --> 42:17.368
[fire crackles]

42:19.119 --> 42:20.746
I should've just gone to Seoul.

42:24.041 --> 42:25.960
Then none of this
would have happened to me.

42:28.212 --> 42:29.505
[Wu-jin] People have always said…

42:31.173 --> 42:33.801
my sister was an archery prodigy
ever since she was little.

42:36.470 --> 42:37.972
So our parents only cared about

42:38.764 --> 42:41.141
trying to get my sister
onto the national team.

42:43.477 --> 42:45.187
They've never paid attention to me at all.

42:47.231 --> 42:49.191
I'll give you all my attention,
brother-in-law.

42:49.942 --> 42:52.528
Don't be sad. You have me.
[groans]

42:55.030 --> 42:56.365
Thank God that I have Dae-su.

43:00.703 --> 43:03.664
I don't really have anything to say.

43:06.292 --> 43:07.793
I wouldn't really know…

43:10.170 --> 43:12.131
but I feel like I made friends.

43:14.258 --> 43:16.343
[soft music]

43:18.887 --> 43:21.181
[fire whooshing]

43:24.435 --> 43:25.603
[sighs]

43:29.523 --> 43:30.608
Me and…

43:32.276 --> 43:33.319
On-jo…

43:34.528 --> 43:36.864
[soft music continues]

43:38.032 --> 43:39.033
[sighs]

43:40.409 --> 43:42.536
[fire crackling]

43:46.457 --> 43:48.584
[suspenseful music]

43:53.547 --> 43:55.299
[distant snarling, approaching footsteps]

43:58.844 --> 44:01.013
[suspenseful music continues]

44:04.975 --> 44:06.894
-[door closes]
-[gasps]

44:09.021 --> 44:10.064
What's that?

44:10.147 --> 44:12.566
-It's… nothing.
-[Gwi-nam] Well…

44:14.943 --> 44:16.570
I have to go to the roof.

44:17.780 --> 44:19.156
But the door's locked.

44:22.493 --> 44:23.827
So I'm going that way.

44:26.372 --> 44:30.542
-You're not a zombie, are you?
-Zombie? Fuck that.

44:31.835 --> 44:33.921
[tense music]

44:35.756 --> 44:36.799
Is that food?

44:36.882 --> 44:38.676
[whimpers]

44:40.844 --> 44:41.804
Are you hungry?

44:44.264 --> 44:45.724
Are you, huh?

44:47.184 --> 44:48.394
Are you hungry?

44:48.477 --> 44:50.479
[tense music continues]

44:55.025 --> 44:55.859
Me too.

44:55.943 --> 44:57.027
[gasps]

44:57.111 --> 44:59.613
-[snarls]
-[groaning]

45:07.746 --> 45:09.998
[discordant music playing]

45:12.000 --> 45:13.961
[squelching]

45:15.462 --> 45:16.922
I just, well…

45:17.923 --> 45:19.591
I just want some water, really.

45:19.675 --> 45:21.677
Not stuff like that.

45:22.636 --> 45:24.138
Be completely honest.

45:25.889 --> 45:28.767
Be completely honest. Do you like someone?

45:28.851 --> 45:31.186
[fire crackling]

45:34.565 --> 45:37.568
-Mm-hm.
-You do? For real?

45:37.651 --> 45:39.987
[gentle music]

45:43.907 --> 45:44.867
Yeah.

45:46.660 --> 45:49.788
Why do you keep on stalling?
Do you have a crush?

45:51.081 --> 45:52.708
Uh, pretty much.

45:53.292 --> 45:54.793
Pretty much? What does that mean?

45:57.463 --> 45:58.464
Who is she?

45:59.631 --> 46:01.967
[gentle music continues]

46:08.515 --> 46:09.683
No one.

46:09.766 --> 46:10.851
Who is she?

46:12.102 --> 46:13.187
Do I know her?

46:15.397 --> 46:16.231
Who is it?

46:17.733 --> 46:18.734
You.

46:20.444 --> 46:21.487
It's you, On-jo.

46:23.405 --> 46:24.531
I like you.

46:27.493 --> 46:30.204
[scoffs]
Hey. Stop that.

46:32.539 --> 46:35.083
He doesn't mean it. He's just kidding.

46:36.710 --> 46:37.544
[soft chuckle]

46:37.628 --> 46:41.298
I mean, we were friends and neighbors
since kindergarten, that's all.

46:41.381 --> 46:43.592
[fire crackling]

46:44.801 --> 46:45.636
Stop joking.

46:47.638 --> 46:48.680
I'm not joking.

46:50.349 --> 46:51.934
Ever since I was six years old,

46:53.560 --> 46:55.270
I've always liked you, On-jo.

46:57.773 --> 46:59.149
And I always will.

46:59.233 --> 47:01.276
[gentle music]

47:04.821 --> 47:05.697
Awesome.

47:09.535 --> 47:10.577
[On-jo groans]

47:22.589 --> 47:24.383
[fire crackling]

47:26.134 --> 47:27.386
Cheong-san.

47:31.765 --> 47:34.142
[gentle music]

47:42.442 --> 47:44.903
[Dae-su] Did you know? I had no idea.

47:44.987 --> 47:46.947
[Hyo-ryeong] You're the only one
who didn't know.

47:47.614 --> 47:49.241
-[Dae-su] Everyone knew?
-[Hyo-ryeong] Yes.

47:50.409 --> 47:52.619
-[Dae-su] Why didn't I know?
-[Wu-jin] I didn't, either.

47:52.703 --> 47:55.205
-[Hyo-ryeong] Because you're you.
-[Wu-jin] Cheong-san's so cool.

47:57.457 --> 47:59.626
[dramatic music]

48:02.087 --> 48:03.171
On-jo.

48:08.719 --> 48:09.636
I'm sorry.

48:12.806 --> 48:14.016
You don't have to like me back.

48:14.099 --> 48:15.100
Please don't.

48:15.183 --> 48:16.184
I did it.

48:18.228 --> 48:19.479
I said it all, so it's all good.

48:20.606 --> 48:22.399
How is it all good? You're a jerk.

48:23.108 --> 48:24.860
You were my best friend.

48:27.988 --> 48:30.157
I-sak's gone and now you're gone too.

48:33.827 --> 48:35.537
What is it that you want from me?

48:38.415 --> 48:40.417
[ominous music]

48:43.128 --> 48:44.087
[slurps]

48:51.094 --> 48:52.429
[sighs]

48:53.305 --> 48:54.640
[slurps]

48:54.723 --> 48:56.725
[foreboding music]

49:04.983 --> 49:07.986
[grunting]

49:11.281 --> 49:12.157
Did you…

49:13.533 --> 49:15.035
Did you ever like me?

49:15.118 --> 49:17.120
[slow music]

49:22.292 --> 49:23.627
Not even a little bit?

49:26.588 --> 49:27.881
You never liked me?

49:32.844 --> 49:34.012
Would you please leave?

49:36.682 --> 49:38.058
I just want to be alone.

49:41.770 --> 49:43.271
You don't have to like me back.

49:47.442 --> 49:49.486
[slow music continues]

49:59.413 --> 50:00.330
[sighs]

50:04.376 --> 50:07.587
[sobbing]

50:08.839 --> 50:10.841
[somber music]

50:17.055 --> 50:19.683
[grunting]

50:25.731 --> 50:26.648
[sighs]

50:26.732 --> 50:28.734
[suspenseful music]

50:36.533 --> 50:37.993
[distant clang]

50:40.746 --> 50:43.248
[suspenseful music rises]

50:44.499 --> 50:46.418
[sudden music sting]

50:48.170 --> 50:50.338
[tense music]

50:55.051 --> 50:56.052
[gasps]

51:01.725 --> 51:03.226
[muffled grunt]

51:03.310 --> 51:04.561
On-jo!

51:04.644 --> 51:06.772
-[tense music rises]
-[On-jo grunts]

51:10.025 --> 51:12.068
-Cheong-san!
-[groaning]

51:17.616 --> 51:19.284
Give me your eye, asshole.

51:20.911 --> 51:22.662
[squishing]

51:22.746 --> 51:25.665
[yelling]

51:25.749 --> 51:27.834
[thunder rumbling]

51:31.880 --> 51:33.882
[closing theme music]

55:20.150 --> 55:25.071
ALL CHARACTERS, LOCATIONS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS SHOW ARE FICTIONAL.
